.SH "NAME"
nvme-feat-voltage-meas \- Get and set voltage measurement feature
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
\fInvme\fR [<global\-options>] \fIfeat voltage\-meas\fR <device>
                        [\-\-act=<action>] [\-\-vssel=<sensor>] [\-\-vmlt]
                        [\-\-svmt=<minutes>] [\-\-luvt=<luvt>] [\-\-lovt=<lovt>]
                        [\-\-sel=<select> | \-S <select>] [\-\-save | \-s]
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
Get and set voltage measurement feature (Feature Identifier 27h), which controls collection of interval voltage measurements for the Voltage Measurement log page\&.
.sp
The <device> parameter is mandatory and may be either the NVMe character device (ex: /dev/nvme0), or a namespace block device (ex: /dev/nvme0n1)\&.
.sp
If any of the setting options are specified, the command issues a Set Features command\&. If none of them are specified, it retrieves and displays the current configuration\&.
.sp
The \-\-vssel, \-\-vmlt, \-\-svmt, \-\-luvt and \-\-lovt options form the Start Voltage Measurements data structure and are only valid with \-\-act=1\&.
.sp
On success it returns 0, error code otherwise\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\-\-act=<action>
.RS 4
Action (ACT): the action the controller takes while processing the command:
.TS
