1
T}:T{
Start voltage measurements
T}
T{
2
T}:T{
Clear the Overvoltage Valid and Undervoltage Valid bits in the Voltage Measurement log page
T}
T{
0xa\-0xf
T}:T{
Vendor specific
T}
.TE
.sp 1
.RE
.PP
\-\-vssel=<sensor>
.RS 4
Voltage Sensor Selected (VSSEL): voltage sensor, 0\-3 (Voltage Sensor 1\-4), used for the interval voltage measurements reported in the Voltage Measurement log page\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-vmlt
.RS 4
Voltage Measurement Log Threshold (VMLT): compare the interval voltage measurements with the thresholds given by
\-\-lovt
and
\-\-luvt\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-svmt=<minutes>
.RS 4
Stop Voltage Measurement Time (SVMT): time in minutes after which the controller stops collecting interval voltage measurements\&. 0 specifies no stop time\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-luvt=<luvt>
.RS 4
Log Undervoltage Threshold (LUVT), 14 bits, in units of the Voltage Sample Scale (VOLSS) reported in the Identify Controller data structure\&. 0 disables the comparison\&. Used only with
\-\-vmlt\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-lovt=<lovt>
.RS 4
Log Overvoltage Threshold (LOVT), 14 bits, in units of the Voltage Sample Scale (VOLSS) reported in the Identify Controller data structure\&. 0 disables the comparison\&. Used only with
\-\-vmlt\&.
.RE
.PP
\-S <select>, \-\-sel=<select>
.RS 4
Select (SEL): This field specifies which value of the attributes to return in the provided data:
